.TH PIPE 2 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
pipe \- create pipe
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, -lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int pipe(int " pipefd [2]);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pipe()
creates a pipe, a unidirectional data channel that can be used for interprocess communication. The array
.I pipefd
is used to return two file descriptors referring to the ends of the pipe.
.I pipefd[0]
refers to the read end of the pipe.
.I pipefd[1]
refers to the write end of the pipe.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned. On error, -1 is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I pipefd
is not valid.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intro(2)
